STARTING TRANSFER LEARNING & BACKBONE BENCHMARK LAB
==================================================

==================================================
TRANSFER LEARNING INTUITION BRIDGE
==================================================
Early CNN Layers (e.g., Conv1, Conv2):
  - Detect low-level visual universal primitives (edges, shapes, circles).
  - These features are highly reusable across ALL image datasets.
Late CNN Layers (e.g., Conv5, Classifier Heads):
  - Detect highly specialized features (cancer anomalies, dog ears, car grills).

Why not train from scratch?
  - Learning edges/shapes from scratch requires thousands of images and hours of compute.
  - Transfer learning reuses pretrained early-layer weights, only updating the specialized
    classification head, saving time and training successfully on tiny datasets.
==================================================

--- PREPROCESSING NORMALIZATION ALIGNMENT ---
ImageNet Normalization Coordinates:
  - mean=[0.485, 0.456, 0.406], std=[0.229, 0.224, 0.225]
  - Assumes natural, everyday outdoor RGB images (dogs, cars, flowers).
Domain Mismatch Warning:
  - When applying transfer learning to specialty domains (e.g., grayscale medical X-rays,
    satellite infrared thermal imaging, microscopic crops), generic parameters
    can lead to color distortions. In custom medical-imaging tasks, computing the
    dataset-specific mean/std first is critical for optimal model convergence.
